## 2. Derived data tables — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

**Applies to the derived tables in `outputs/` that carry DDInter content.**

DDInter's download data are published under
[CC BY-NC-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/) —
**non-commercial** and **ShareAlike**. No raw DDInter download is committed to
this repository (`src/ingest/fetch_ddinter.py` retrieves it, and
`data/` is gitignored), but several committed tables are *adaptations* of it
because they carry DDInter drug names, DDInter severity grades, or statistics
computed directly from them.

Files that inherit CC BY-NC-SA 4.0:

| File | Why |
|---|---|
| `outputs/policy_assignments.parquet` | DDInter drug-pair names and severity grades on every row |
| `outputs/burden_by_pair.csv` | DDInter pair names and severities |
| `outputs/burden_by_severity.csv` | Aggregates over DDInter severity |
| `outputs/ingredient_mapping.csv` | The RxNorm → DDInter name bridge |
| `outputs/alert_budget_table.csv`, `outputs/r_*.csv` | Statistics computed from DDInter severity |

**What that means for reuse.** You may share and adapt these tables for
non-commercial purposes, with attribution, and any adaptation must be released
under the same licence. Commercial use is not permitted by the upstream licence,
and this repository cannot grant it.

**Attribution for the interaction data:**

> Xiong G, et al. *DDInter: an online drug–drug interaction database towards
> improving clinical decision-making and patient safety.* Nucleic Acids Research
> 2022; 50(D1):D1200–D1207.
>
> Updated in: *DDInter 2.0: an enhanced drug interaction resource with expanded
> data coverage, new interaction types, and improved user interface.* Nucleic
> Acids Research 2025; 53(D1):D1356–D1362.
>
> Data retrieved 2026-09-07 from https://ddinter.scbdd.com/download/ under
> CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

Retrieval details, file hashes and row counts are recorded in
`data/raw/ddinter/MANIFEST.json`, produced by the fetch script.

---

## 3. Upstream sources and their terms

| Source | Used for | Licence / terms |
|---|---|---|
| [Synthea](https://github.com/synthetichealth/synthea) | Synthetic patients, prescriptions, conditions | Apache 2.0. Output is synthetic; **no real patient data is involved anywhere in this project.** |
| [RxNorm / RxNav](https://rxnav.nlm.nih.gov/) (US NLM) | Ingredient-level normalisation | Free public API, no account required. RxNorm is subject to the [UMLS licence](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/umls/knowledge_sources/metathesaurus/release/license_agreement.html) for bulk redistribution; only derived ingredient mappings are committed here. |
| [DDInter](https://ddinter.scbdd.com/) | Interaction pairs and severity | **CC BY-NC-SA 4.0** — see section 2. |

**Deliberately excluded on licence grounds**, and recorded in `NOTES.md`:

- **DrugBank** — licence restricts redistribution.
- **TWOSIDES** — licence unspecified on Therapeutics Data Commons, so not
  redistributed.

---

## 4. Scope note

Nothing in this repository is clinically validated, and no part of it should be
used to make treatment decisions. See the "Not an adverse-event prediction
model" callout at the top of `README.md` and section 13 of `eval/criteria.md`
for what this analysis can and cannot establish.

This file records the licensing position as understood by the author from the
upstream terms cited above. It is not legal advice; if you intend to reuse the
derived tables commercially, take the question to DDInter directly.
